{"kind":"stack","id":"s-magnets","title":"Magnets: attract, repel and materials","theme":{"background":"#0f172a","foreground":"#f8fafc","font":"Verdana, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-term","content":"Magnet"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-expl","content":"An object that pulls some metals towards it. It has a north pole and a south pole."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-term","content":"Attract"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-expl","content":"To pull towards something. Opposite poles of two magnets attract each other."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","id":"c3-pic","picto":"magnet"},{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"What happens when the north pole of one magnet meets the south pole of another?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"They pull together","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"They push apart","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Nothing happens","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"What happens when two north poles are brought together?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"They push apart","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"They pull together","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"They stick permanently","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-d","label":"They turn into one magnet","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","id":"c5-pic","picto":"coin"},{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"Which material will a magnet attract?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Wood","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Plastic","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"Iron","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-q","content":"You find a magnet in the science box. Do you test it on a steel spoon or a plastic ruler?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"Test the steel spoon","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Test the plastic ruler","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"The magnet sticks to the spoon. Steel contains iron, so magnets attract it."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"The magnet does not stick to the ruler. Plastic is not a magnetic material, so the magnet does not attract it."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Which of these is NOT attracted by a magnet?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Paper clip","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Glass jar","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"Steel nail","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-h","content":"Well done! You finished the magnets lesson."},{"type":"text","id":"c10-m","content":"You now know that opposite poles attract, like poles repel, and magnets pull on iron and steel but not on wood or plastic."}],"actions":[{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"}]}}
